      <section class="scp-workflow" aria-labelledby="scp-workflow-title">
        <div class="scp-section-heading">
          <p class="scp-eyebrow">A workflow that stays connected</p>
          <h2 id="scp-workflow-title">Move from instrument files to defensible results.</h2>
          <p>Use individual tools when you need precision, or compose them into a complete analysis pipeline with datasets, units, metadata, and plots kept together.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scp-stage-grid">
          <a class="scp-stage scp-stage-import" href="userguide/importexport/index.html"><span class="scp-stage-mark">01</span><strong>Import and organize</strong><span>Read experimental data while preserving coordinates and metadata.</span><b>Formats and I/O <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></b></a>
          <a class="scp-stage scp-stage-process" href="userguide/processing/index.html"><span class="scp-stage-mark">02</span><strong>Process with intent</strong><span>Correct baselines, filter noise, transform signals, and document each step.</span><b>Processing tools <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></b></a>
          <a class="scp-stage scp-stage-analyze" href="userguide/analysis/index.html"><span class="scp-stage-mark">03</span><strong>Analyze and model</strong><span>Explore patterns with multivariate analysis, decomposition, and fitting.</span><b>Analysis methods <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></b></a>
          <a class="scp-stage scp-stage-plot" href="userguide/plotting/index.html"><span class="scp-stage-mark">04</span><strong>Visualize clearly</strong><span>Create publication-ready figures that stay linked to the data behind them.</span><b>Plotting guide <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></b></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="scp-community" class="scp-paths scp-community" aria-labelledby="scp-community-title">
        <div class="scp-paths-heading"><p class="scp-eyebrow">Research and community</p><h2 id="scp-community-title">Science grows when we share it.</h2></div>
        <div class="scp-path-grid">
          <article class="scp-path">
            <span>Research in practice</span>
            <h3>How people use SpectroChemPy</h3>
            <p>Explore papers citing SpectroChemPy, from operando FTIR in catalysis to materials characterization and biomedical Raman spectroscopy.</p>
            <div class="scp-community-links"><a href="reference/papers.html">Explore the publications <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
          </article>
          <article class="scp-path">
            <span>A connected toolbox</span>
            <h3>Built to be extended</h3>
            <p>Go further with plugins for NMR, tensor methods, and instrument formats, and discover the wider scientific Python ecosystem.</p>
            <div class="scp-community-links"><a href="userguide/plugins/index.html">Discover the plugins <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a><a href="credits/seealso.html">Explore related projects <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
          </article>
          <article class="scp-path">
            <span>Take part</span>
            <h3>Cite it, share it, improve it</h3>
            <p>Using SpectroChemPy in your research? Find the citation and BibTeX entry, share an example, or help improve the project.</p>
            <div class="scp-community-links"><a href="credits/citing.html">Cite SpectroChemPy <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a><a href="devguide/index.html">Ways to contribute <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

